.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH AMU 8
.SH NAME
amu \- Qwaderton Linux package manager frontend (command router)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBamu\fR is the central command-line frontend for package management on
Qwaderton Linux. It does no work itself; based on the first option or
subcommand it exec-delegates to one of the backend tools and passes all
remaining arguments through unchanged. It never invokes \fBspm\fR(8)
directly; \fBamu\-bin\fR(8) is the only tool that operates on packages
and the spm database.
.TP
\fBamu\-src\fR(8)
source builds and recipe utilities: \fB\-w\fR (download source),
\fB\-p\fR (print recipe path), \fB\-g\fR (update \fI.shasum\fR),
\fB\-k\fR (update \fI.files\fR), \fB\-s\fR (repo search).
.TP
\fBamu\-bin\fR(8)
package management: \fB\-i\fR (install), \fB\-u\fR (upgrade),
\fB\-r\fR (remove), \fB\-R\fR (remove with unneeded dependencies),
\fB\-U\fR (system upgrade), \fB\-Q\fR (query installed),
\fB\-l\fR (list files), \fB\-O\fR (file owner).
.TP
\fBamu\-resolv\fR(8)
dependency graph queries: \fB\-d\fR, \fB\-dd\fR, \fB\-D\fR, \fB\-DD\fR,
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-jj\fR.
.TP
\fBamu\-trigger\fR(8)
post-install system cache/database triggers.

.SH ROUTING TABLE
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
\fBfirst option\fR|\fBbackend\fR|\fBaction\fR
_
\-w, \-p, \-g, \-k|amu\-src|source build utilities
\-s|amu\-bin|repo search
\-d, \-dd|amu\-resolv|direct dependencies
\-D, \-DD|amu\-resolv|dependency closure
\-j, \-jj|amu\-resolv|dependents
\-r, \-R|amu\-bin|remove
\-U|amu\-bin|system upgrade
\-o, \-c|amu\-bin|download, cache clean
\-Q, \-l, \-O|amu\-bin|installed package queries
\-i, \-u|(see below)|install/upgrade
.TE

.SH CONTEXT ROUTING
.TP
No arguments
If the current directory contains an \fIabuild\fR recipe file, the call
is routed to \fBamu\-src\fR and the package is built from source.
Otherwise the help message is printed.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR and \fB\-u\fR
The router inspects the arguments and decides whether to build from
source or to install a pre-built binary:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
an argument naming an existing \fI.spm\fR file is routed to
\fBamu\-bin\fR, which installs/upgrades the file directly;
.IP \(bu 2
an argument naming a package that has a recipe in \fBAMU_REPO\fR is
routed to \fBamu\-src\fR, which builds the package and then hands the
resulting \fI.spm\fR to \fBamu\-bin\fR for installation;
.IP \(bu 2
an argument naming a package with no recipe is routed to
\fBamu\-bin\fR, which downloads the binary from \fBAMU_BINREPO\fR;
.IP \(bu 2
with no arguments and an \fIabuild\fR file in the current directory,
the current recipe is built and installed.
.RE

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
\fBamu trigger\fR [pkg...]|run post-install triggers
\fBamu purge\fR [--do-it] pkg...|removal plan for pkg plus unneeded deps
\fBamu orphan\fR|installed packages without dependents
\fBamu foreign\fR|installed packages missing from repos
\fBamu mdpurge\fR [--do-it] [pkg...]|orphaned makedepends (all if no pkg)
\fBamu clean\fR [\-p] [\-s]|stale .spm files or sources on stdout
\fBamu deps\fR pkg|runtime library dependencies via ldd(1)
\fBamu redundantdeps\fR [\-f] [pkg]|transitive deps listed in depends
\fBamu genabuild\fR url [name]|scaffold a recipe directory from a URL
\fBamu revdep\fR [\-v]|packages with broken ELF library links
.TE
.LP
\fBamu purge\fR and \fBamu mdpurge\fR print the removal plan by default;
pass \fB\-\-do\-it\fR to actually remove (via \fBamu\-bin\fR).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.LP
Configuration is passed through to the backend tools. See
\fBamu\-src\fR(8) (\fBAMU_REPO\fR, \fBAMU_PACKAGE_DIR\fR,
\fBAMU_SOURCE_DIR\fR, \fBAMU_WORK_DIR\fR, \fBAMU_ROOT\fR,
\fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR, \fBAMU_KEEP_WORKDIR\fR), \fBamu\-bin\fR(8)
(\fBAMU_BINREPO\fR, \fBAMU_CACHE_DIR\fR, \fBAMU_MASK\fR,
\fBAMU_ALIAS\fR, \fBAMU_STRICT\fR) and \fBamu\-resolv\fR(8).
System-wide defaults are read from \fI/etc/amu.conf\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
.LP
Install a package by name (build from source if a recipe exists,
otherwise download the binary):
.RS
\f(CRamu \-i firefox\fR
.RE
.LP
Install a pre-built package file:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-i firefox#128.0\-1.spm\fR
.RE
.LP
Build and install the recipe in the current directory:
.RS
\f(CRcd repo/mypkg && amu \-i\fR
.RE
.LP
Full system upgrade:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-U\fR
.RE
.LP
Remove a package together with its unneeded dependencies:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-R firefox\fR
.RE
.LP
Show the dependency tree of a package:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-DD firefox\fR
.RE
.LP
List all installed packages:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-Q\fR
.RE
.LP
Find which installed package owns a file:
.RS
\f(CRamu \-O /usr/lib/libpng.so\fR
.RE
.LP
Preview then perform a purge:
.RS
\f(CRamu purge firefox\fR
.br
\f(CRamu purge \-\-do\-it firefox\fR
.RE

